            <ArticleTitle>Hysterectomy for Benign Conditions of the Uterus: Total Vaginal Hysterectomy.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>441-62</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.ogc.2016.04.004</ELocationID>
            <ELocationID EIdType="pii" ValidYN="Y">S0889-8545(16)30006-7</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>As minimally invasive technology continues to be developed and refined, surgeons must be discerning in choosing the safest, cost-effective surgical approach associated with the best outcomes for each individual patient. Vaginal hysterectomy can be successfully accomplished even in challenging situations, such as previous pelvic surgery, nulliparity, uterine enlargement, or obesity. Vaginal hysterectomy should be considered the primary route for treatment of benign disease.</AbstractText>
